  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n(7, 9, 48)\n\n__(7 + 9)__ × 3 = 48 \n\n**__16 __**__**× 3**__ = 48\n\n48 = 48 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n(6, 8, 42)\n\n__(6 + 8)__ × 3 = 42 \n\n__14 ____× 3__ = 42\n\n42 = 42 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo, checking each option one by one:\n\nOption 1) (8, 10, 47)\n\n__(8 + 10)__ × 3 = 47 \n\n__18 ____× 3__ = 47\n\n54 ≠ 47 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 2) (9, 11, 56)\n\n__(9 + 11)__ × 3 = 56 \n\n__20 ____× 3__ = 56\n\n60 ≠ 56 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nOption 3) (11, 13, 72)\n\n__(11 + 13)__ × 3 = 72 \n\n__24 ____× 3__ = 72\n\n72 = 72 (LHS = RHS)\n\nOption 4) (10, 12, 54)\n\n__(10 + 12)__ × 3 = 54 \n\n__22 ____× 3__ = 54\n\n66 ≠ 54 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nThus, out of all the options, '(11, 13, 72)' follows the same logic as given.\n\nHence, \"Option 3\" is the correct answer.",
